description:
Reproduced 2026-10-03: `spk verify specs` reports 7 files properties_uncompilable (was 0 before Revision 15 — pre-rjb every file was properties_failed, i.e. scratch COMPILED and failed at run). Regression introduced by the rjb emission change.

Root cause: Property rows whose generator cell yields no `pat in strategy` params (e.g. linter-schema_shape.md's generators like `(revision_n, revision_n_plus_1) where a member was removed from a variant table...`) are emitted as PARAMETERLESS blocks INSIDE the proptest! macro:

    proptest! {
        fn shrunk_id_set_rejected() { todo_predicate!("..."); }
    }

proptest! requires every fn to carry `(pat in strategy)` params — a bare `fn name()` inside the macro is a parse error ("expected expression, found keyword fn", 4 errors in linter-schema_shape_props.rs alone; reproduced standalone with a probe crate). The old emission kept these compiling.

Impact: 7/22 corpus files can't even reach "honest failure" — the scratch can't run at all, so verify's verdict for them is uncompilable, worse than the todo-panic failure it replaced.

RED: test compiling the emitted props for a spec with a parameterless-generator row (fixture: generator cell text with no `in`) — must compile.

GREEN: emit parameterless blocks OUTSIDE proptest! as plain #[test] fns (still honest via todo_predicate! / assert! bodies), or emit them as proptest blocks over a unit strategy — pick the one that keeps law-case splitting intact. Keep fragment rows unchanged.
